        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T16:17:17Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): the tool library window shows the tool as an orbitable 3D model and a to-scale side view\n\nThe editor of the tool library window gets a preview area above its\ntabs with two views and a toggle:\n- 3D (the default): the tool as an orbitable model. A tool with a\n  landed body shows the steel revolved up to the body and the body's own\n  facets; a tool without one shows the steel and the holder cylinder\n  revolved, so the view is never empty. The steel is the landed drawn\n  cutter (carried onto the draft numbers), else Tool::profile.\n- Side: the to-scale side drawing with dimension lines (diameter, flute\n  length, shank, stick-out, gauge, holder diameter x length).\n\nThe body placement view's renderer moves into tool_model_view.rs, which\nboth views use; Pick tip / Pick axis keep working. The Properties\npreview shows a landed drawn cutter outside \"Draw cutter\" (#93 leftover).\nThe model and the projected screen mesh are cached on their inputs; a\nstill frame builds and projects nothing.\n\nFixes #3894\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
